    Used: the message formats and the rules the tests check. RFC 1122, whose §3.2.2 the tests also check,
    is in ../arp/rfc1122.txt.

linux.txt
    Frames that the Linux kernel (7.0.14-linuxkit, of Docker Desktop on arm64, with the tools of Debian
    trixie) sent between four network namespaces on 2026-10-26: a host, a router (with radvd sending
    Router Advertisements) and a second router on the host's link, and a host behind the router on a link
    of an MTU of 1,280 (576 for IPv4 by a route). Echoes, Time Exceeded (TTL, hop limit, reassembly),
    Fragmentation Needed and Packet Too Big, Port and Protocol Unreachable, Redirect, Parameter Problem
    (an unknown next header, an unknown option), Router Solicitation and Advertisement, Neighbor
    Solicitation and Advertisement (with duplicate address detection), MLDv2, and the multi-part
    extensions of RFC 4884 that Linux adds to errors (net.ipv4.icmp_errors_extension_mask). The frames of
    the host's link come first, then those of the far link. Checksum offloading was turned off.
    Each frame is a line of hexadecimal after "# " lines with tcpdump's summary of it (`tcpdump -n -e -v`).
    Made by linux.sh, run as `docker run --rm --privileged -v "$PWD":/out debian:trixie sh /out/linux.sh`,
    and `python3 ../ethernet/linux.py` on lan.pcap and far.pcap with their summaries, the outputs joined.
    License: produced for this project (no third-party content).
